    "Model exhibits severe upward bias during high volatility regimes; forecasts consistently overestimate price levels by 5-10% when recent history shows a spike (e.g., >64 EUR).",
    "Forecasts fail to capture mean reversion after sharp spikes, assuming linear continuation while true outcomes show immediate reversal and extended consolidation.",
    "Sentiment signals (0.33/0.20) are ignored by the model; low sentiment periods coincide with forecast errors where price drops below historical averages.",
    "Model demonstrates significant lag in reacting to volatility clusters, smoothing out rapid swings that result in systematic underestimation of downside risk and overestimation of upside potential.",
    "In high-volatility windows (e.g., Oct 2021), the model's 30-day horizon is structurally flawed, predicting a flat trend instead of the observed 'spike-and-fall' pattern."
